Network Orchestrator includes the unmodified Xray-core v26.10.31 Linux binary.
Release and source: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/releases/tag/v26.10.31
License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (see the accompanying LICENSE file).

The hash-pinned geoip.dat and geosite.dat are from that Xray-core release.
Its scheduled-assets-update workflow obtains GeoIP Lite and GeoSite Standard
from XTLS/Xray-rules-dat:
https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-rules-dat
https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/blob/v26.10.31/.github/workflows/scheduled-assets-update.yml
The data project is licensed as a whole under GPL-3.0:
https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-rules-dat/blob/main/LICENSE
On Debian and Ubuntu the GPL-3.0 text is at /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3;
on Arch it is at /usr/share/licenses/common/GPL3/license.
Corresponding source, data sources, and build instructions:
https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-rules-dat/blob/geoip/README.md
https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-rules-dat/blob/geosite/README.md
GeoIP is based on IPinfo Lite (https://ipinfo.io/lite), supplemented with
regional-routing and service data. GeoSite includes domain-list-community data.
The project's README documents its additional upstream datasets and notices.

